WEBVTT

NOTE Silent video. Cues are the on-screen step captions; the terminal text is in the transcript.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.100
file: is a URL now: The manifest lives in another repo. A public one needs no token: a URL and the keys it owns.

2
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:16.267
validate fetches it: The merged object is checked. billing's bad ticket is reported at the URL, line 6, not in the page.

3
00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:28.900
Private: add tokenEnv: tokenEnv names the variable holding the token. Unset, the run stops with exit 2 and names the variable.

4
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:35.233
--offline refuses it: A remote manifest is fetched every run, never cached. With no network there is nothing to check, so it stops.

5
00:00:35.233 --> 00:00:40.233
Exit codes for CI: 1 for findings, 2 when the manifest cannot be reached. The message names the variable, never the token.

